-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107, after review: a deadline that names an imported rule
-- is held to what that rule reads, as one naming a rule of the file is. Each
-- of these used to be worked out outside a run: `ledger duty` as 10, against
-- an empty ledger; `clock duty` and `library clock duty` (the standard
-- library's `Today serial`) by the day the command ran; `env duty` from the
-- command's environment; `window duty` at `rate`'s TYPICALLY default, 30.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT readers
IMPORT `excel-date`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`ledger duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `recorded period` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`clock duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `clocky` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`library clock duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN (`Today serial` MODULO 7) PLUS 3 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`env duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `env period` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`window duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `the window` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
